  "term": "muscarinic receptor",
  "definition": "A muscarinic receptor is a cell receptor that responds to acetylcholine. In this source, the M3 muscarinic receptor is described as activating PKC and p38 MAPK signaling, which increased miR-222 expression and cell proliferation, and its effects were blocked by atropine.",
