      "passed": false,
      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that acetylcholine acting through M3 muscarinic receptor signaling stimulates PKC/p38 MAPK pathways, increases miR-222 expression, and promotes proliferation, but the definition overstates this as if the receptor itself is directly described as \"activating\" those pathways in the source.",
        "The statement that \"its effects were blocked by atropine\" is too broad: the packet says atropine attenuated ACh-induced pri-miR-222 increases and blocked ACh-induced proliferation, but not all downstream effects (for example, it did not block miR-222 mimics or the PKC agonist condition).",
        "The definition compresses multiple experimental conditions into a single generalized claim, which is not fully supported by the source wording."
